 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 506973,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A sequence is known to be arithmetic. Two of the terms are <span data-math=\"{a_{14}} = 41\">{a_{14}} = 41</span> and <span data-math=\"{a_{38}} = 161\">{a_{38}} = 161</span> . Use that information to find the constant difference and the first term. Then determine the <span data-math=\"{151\\text{st}}\">{151\\text{st}}</span> term of the sequence.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"{a_{14}} = 41,{a_{38}} = 161\"></span></p>\n<p>When you know two terms, you can find the constant difference using this formula: <span data-math=\"d = \\frac{{{a_j} - {a_i}}}{{j - i}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"d = \\frac{{161 - 41}}{{38 - 14}} = \\frac{{120}}{{24}} = 5\"></span></p>\n<p>The first term in the sequence can be found using this formula: <span data-math=\"{a_1} = {a_i} - d\\left({i - 1} \\right)\"></span> and <span data-math=\"{a_{14}} = 41\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{a_1} = 41 - 5\\left({14 - 1} \\right) = 41 - 5(13) = 41 - 65 = - 24\"></span></p>\n<p>The 151st term can be found using this formula: <span data-math=\"{a_i} = {a_1} + d \\times \\left({i - 1} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{a_{151}} = - 24 + 5 \\times \\left({151 - 1} \\right) = - 24 + 5(150) = - 24 + 750 = 726\"></span></p>\n<p>The constant difference is 5, the first term is <span data-math=\"-24,\"></span> and the 151st term is 726.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"d = 5\">d = 5</span>, <span data-math=\"{a_1} =  - 24\">{a_1} =  - 24</span> , and <span data-math=\"{a_{151}} = 726\">{a_{151}} = 726</span>"
    }
   ],
